From: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 13:37:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] udf: Fix bh leak for unallocated space entries
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.61
Git-commit: d95094d4c0a62ea17b8a7c6399b42381b8a55bc0

[ Upstream commit d95094d4c0a62ea17b8a7c6399b42381b8a55bc0 ]

When processing unallocated space entries we didn't properly release the
inode bh. Fix it.

Signed-off-by: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 fs/udf/inode.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/fs/udf/inode.c b/fs/udf/inode.c
index 6a0c66d70629..84b1a0b7b28d 100644
--- a/fs/udf/inode.c
+++ b/fs/udf/inode.c
@@ -1495,6 +1495,7 @@ static int udf_read_inode(struct inode *inode, bool hidden_inode)
 		memcpy(iinfo->i_data,
 		       bh->b_data + sizeof(struct unallocSpaceEntry),
 		       bs - sizeof(struct unallocSpaceEntry));
+		brelse(bh);
 		return 0;
 	}
 
-- 
2.56.0

